anent Driving Licence: After a minimum of 30 days from the issue of the learner’s licence, you can book a practical driving test with your local Regional Transport Office (RTO) to get your permanent licence.", "reference_indexes": [2, 3]}, {"snippet": "Official Portal: Applications and status checks are handled digitally through the official Parivahan Sewa Portal .", "snippet_links": [{"text": "Parivahan Sewa Portal", "link": "https://parivahan.gov.in/en/faq/new-driver-license-services"}], "reference_indexes": [4]}], "reference_indexes": [0, 1]}, {"type": "paragraph", "snippet": "If you would like, I can guide you through the document checklist (such as age and address proof) or explain the steps to apply for a learner's licence online ."}], "references": [{"index": 0, "title": "Types of Driving Licence in India", "link": "https://www.bajajfinserv.in/insurance/types-of-driving-licence", "snippet": "Types of Driving Licence in India * Eligibility criteria for driving licence in India To be eligible for a driving licence in India, applicants must meet the follo...", "source": "Bajaj Finserv", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://www.bajajfinserv.in&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL"}, {"index": 1, "title": "Different Types of Driving Licences and Who Can Apply", "link": "https://www.hdfcergo.com/blogs/car-insurance/different-types-of-driving-licences-and-who-can-apply", "snippet": "Types of Driving Licences in India Licence Categories Explained: Pick What Fits Your Ride Because there are so many types of cars on the road, the transport author...", "source": "HDFC ERGO General Insurance", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://www.hdfcergo.com&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL", "thumbnail": "https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRMiFBFyNe_uJAyGJO4xNr_GMiYSJS4mECyPHKE8fGmCPLhdZUgavpPUQm1jjhI3e6CYvcg1PAt285fPTwSYLrSTbLmqJv-1vdeO96j"